Your heart doesnt beat perfectly regularly, the intervals between beats naturally fluctuate to reflect your bodys ability to adjust to changing physiological and environmental demands. 
What HRV Score Measures
HRV quantifies the precise timing variation between successive interbeat (RR) intervals. For example, consecutive beats might measure 950 milliseconds, 1,020 milliseconds, 980 milliseconds, and 1,050 milliseconds.
These changes are partly influenced by the autonomic nervous system (ANS), which continuously adjusts cardiovascular function in response to internal and external demands.
What HRV score measures includes:
Beat-to-beat timing variations
Autonomic nervous system regulation
Your bodys ability to adapt to stress and recovery
Parasympathetic and sympathetic nervous system balance

HRV shows how your nervous system is working. But dont use it to measure stress. And dont use it alone to diagnose problems
